CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member, array: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ replacement, array: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ noexcept\(false\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Deallocation functions without a noexcept-specifier were taken as
potentially-throwing.  clang++ 18 agrees with [except.spec]/9; g++ 13
does not (it reports the first assertion failing).
